From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 06 Mar 2026 11:53:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: fix netdev registration after wiphy_register

brcmf_net_attach() with locked=false calls register_netdev(), which
acquires only rtnl_lock.  After brcmf_cfg80211_attach() has called
wiphy_register(), every netdev with ieee80211_ptr set must be registered
through cfg80211_register_netdevice() so that wdev->registered is set
to true *before* register_netdevice() runs.  This suppresses the
NETDEV_REGISTER notifier's cfg80211_register_wdev() path (which requires
wiphy_lock) and prevents a race where the wdev can end up partially
registered.

On BCM4330 SDIO (AP6330 / Cubieboard4) the race is reliably hit at
boot: brcmf_fweh_activate_events() is called inside
brcmf_cfg80211_attach(), and a firmware E_IF event can fire and call
brcmf_net_attach() concurrently.  The second brcmf_net_attach() then
calls register_netdev() on an already-registered ndev, triggering

  kernel BUG at net/core/dev.c:10174
  BUG_ON(dev->reg_state != NETREG_UNINITIALIZED)

This also permanently deadlocks rtnl_lock, causing any subsequent
`ip a` / `ip link` to hang.

Fix: when locked=false acquire rtnl_lock + wiphy_lock and always call
cfg80211_register_netdevice(), matching the expected locking contract
for cfg80211-backed interfaces.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c	2026-03-06 13:13:24.384412308 +0200
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c	2026-03-06 13:14:26.367664639 +0200
@@ -638,12 +638,14 @@
 int brcmf_net_attach(struct brcmf_if *ifp, bool locked)
 {
 	struct brcmf_pub *drvr = ifp->drvr;
+	struct wiphy *wiphy;
 	struct net_device *ndev;
 	s32 err;
 
 	brcmf_dbg(TRACE, "Enter, bsscfgidx=%d mac=%pM\n", ifp->bsscfgidx,
 		  ifp->mac_addr);
 	ndev = ifp->ndev;
+	wiphy = cfg_to_wiphy(drvr->config);
 
 	/* set appropriate operations */
 	ndev->netdev_ops = &brcmf_netdev_ops_pri;
@@ -658,10 +660,24 @@
 	INIT_WORK(&ifp->multicast_work, _brcmf_set_multicast_list);
 	INIT_WORK(&ifp->ndoffload_work, _brcmf_update_ndtable);
 
-	if (locked)
-		err = cfg80211_register_netdevice(ndev);
-	else
-		err = register_netdev(ndev);
+	/*
+	 * After wiphy_register() the ndev has ieee80211_ptr set. All
+	 * registration must go through cfg80211_register_netdevice() so
+	 * that wdev->registered is marked true before register_netdevice()
+	 * runs, preventing the NETDEV_REGISTER notifier from calling
+	 * cfg80211_register_wdev() without wiphy_lock held (which can
+	 * race and leave the device in a broken state, causing a kernel
+	 * BUG at net/core/dev.c: reg_state != NETREG_UNINITIALIZED).
+	 */
+	if (!locked) {
+		rtnl_lock();
+		wiphy_lock(wiphy);
+	}
+	err = cfg80211_register_netdevice(ndev);
+	if (!locked) {
+		wiphy_unlock(wiphy);
+		rtnl_unlock();
+	}
 	if (err != 0) {
 		bphy_err(drvr, "couldn't register the net device\n");
 		goto fail;
